- [Greta] Come here.

1256
00:49:03,042 --> 00:49:05,743
- Spread out Sabu
three's a crowd.

1257
00:49:05,743 --> 00:49:07,278
- [Greta] Sit down.

1258
00:49:07,278 --> 00:49:09,513
- [Tom] Can I order right
away I'm really famished?

1259
00:49:13,285 --> 00:49:14,485
- [Joel] Coast is clear.

1260
00:49:14,485 --> 00:49:16,287
- Did my father
send you to find me?

1261
00:49:16,287 --> 00:49:19,390
- Well not exactly
Miss Vanderhorn.

1262
00:49:19,390 --> 00:49:21,225
- What do you mean not exactly?

1263
00:49:21,225 --> 00:49:22,527
- Your father's dead.

1264
00:49:22,527 --> 00:49:23,695
- [Joel] And my mom?

1265
00:49:24,528 --> 00:49:25,730
- Whoops.

1266
00:49:25,730 --> 00:49:28,767
(soft music)

1267
00:49:28,767 --> 00:49:29,668
- When did he die?

1268
00:49:30,735 --> 00:49:32,037
- Not quite a month ago.

1269
00:49:32,037 --> 00:49:34,272
- [Tom] My partner shot him too.

1270
00:49:34,272 --> 00:49:36,708
(soft music)

1271
00:49:40,978 --> 00:49:42,913
- Well I guess you
can throw that away.

1272
00:49:45,350 --> 00:49:47,252
- [Joel] Oh it just
came with the frame,

1273
00:49:47,252 --> 00:49:49,387
queer looking old duff.

1274
00:49:49,387 --> 00:49:51,990
- Never lived to find
out what happened to me.

1275
00:49:51,990 --> 00:49:54,158
- Exactly what did happen?

1276
00:49:54,158 --> 00:49:56,562
- [Tom] Okay, here it goes, I
was paging through the dailies

1277
00:49:56,562 --> 00:49:58,730
and I seen an opening
for a jungle goddess.

1278
00:50:00,032 --> 00:50:02,767
- At Hastings on the Hudson.

1279
00:50:02,767 --> 00:50:05,570
- [Tom] Meanwhile at
Stately Way Manor.

1280
00:50:08,573 --> 00:50:11,008
Miss Harcourt's
School for Girls,

1281
00:50:13,845 --> 00:50:15,280
chicks on beds.

1282
00:50:15,280 --> 00:50:17,048
- [Greta] It was Sunday
morning September the 1, 1939.

1283
00:50:17,048 --> 00:50:19,217
I was listening to the
radio with my roommate,

1284
00:50:19,217 --> 00:50:20,652
Helen Phillips.

1285
00:50:20,652 --> 00:50:22,720
- [Announcer] In general the
world picture remains the same.

1286
00:50:22,720 --> 00:50:23,922
Although the threat of war is.

1287
00:50:23,922 --> 00:50:25,390
- She had a really deep voice.

1288
00:50:25,390 --> 00:50:26,558
- [Announcer] One moment
please ladies and gentlemen,

1289
00:50:26,558 --> 00:50:28,293
I've just been
handed the teletype.

1290
00:50:28,293 --> 00:50:29,795
Prime Minister Nevil Chamberlain

1291
00:50:29,795 --> 00:50:32,230
has just addressed Parliament
and I quote his exact words.

1292
00:50:32,230 --> 00:50:33,765
- [All] Help!

1293
00:50:33,765 --> 00:50:35,200
- [Announcer] "I just wanted
to inform you that unless"

1294
00:50:35,200 --> 00:50:37,468
"the German government suspends
all aggressive actions"

1295
00:50:37,468 --> 00:50:39,137
"against Poland, not later than"

1296
00:50:39,137 --> 00:50:42,107
"11:00 a.m. British
Summit time September 3,"

1297
00:50:42,107 --> 00:50:45,310
"his Majesty's government
will without hesitation"

1298
00:50:45,310 --> 00:50:47,778
"fulfill it's
obligations to Poland."

1299
00:50:50,015 --> 00:50:52,717
- [Tom] Well that's good Helen,
now try opening with a joke.

1300
00:50:52,717 --> 00:50:54,618
- What are you doing
that for Greta?

1301
00:50:54,618 --> 00:50:56,522
- I don't wanna hear anymore.

1302
00:50:56,522 --> 00:50:58,323
- [Tom] Those morning
look just great on me.

1303
00:50:58,323 --> 00:51:01,693
- So what this is the
United States remember?

1304
00:51:01,693 --> 00:51:03,562
Who cares what's
going on in Europe?

1305
00:51:03,562 --> 00:51:05,097
- [Tom] I'm rich with
no political standing.

1306
00:51:05,097 --> 00:51:06,632
- Oh I'm sorry Greta
I forgot you're dutch.

1307
00:51:06,632 --> 00:51:09,633
- Oh that's alright, I'll
have to see Miss Harcourt.

1308
00:51:09,633 --> 00:51:11,035
- [Roommate] What
are you gonna do?

1309
00:51:11,035 --> 00:51:12,237
- I'm going to take
the first plane home

1310
00:51:12,237 --> 00:51:13,805
if I can make reservations.

1311
00:51:13,805 --> 00:51:15,773
- But why you're safe here?

1312
00:51:15,773 --> 00:51:18,042
- That's beside the point, I
don't want to be stuck here

1313
00:51:18,042 --> 00:51:20,578
for the duration, and
if the war breaks.

1314
00:51:20,578 --> 00:51:23,047
Well maybe I'll be a
nurse, my first aid course

1315
00:51:23,047 --> 00:51:24,515
might come in handy.

1316
00:51:24,515 --> 00:51:26,217
- Oh it sounds like a lot of
cooky fun, we'll put on a show.

1317
00:51:26,217 --> 00:51:30,455
And once the B2 turns into
guava jelly I'll still be alive.

1318
00:51:30,455 --> 00:51:32,657
- Johannesburg is in
a British dominion.

1319
00:51:32,657 --> 00:51:36,360
And if war breaks well I, I
want to be with my father.

1320
00:51:39,297 --> 00:51:40,832
- [Tom] Avril Herrimen?

1321
00:51:42,633 --> 00:51:43,668
- It's Adolph Majou.

1322
00:51:43,668 --> 00:51:44,903
- [Joel] Yeah I think so.

1323
00:51:47,405 --> 00:51:49,808
- [Greta] After considerable
red tape, I was able to.

1324
00:51:49,808 --> 00:51:51,342
- [Tom] I went on some bombing
raids over central Europe.

1325
00:51:51,342 --> 00:51:54,012
- [Greta] Which was the most
direct route to South Africa.

1326
00:51:55,680 --> 00:51:58,317
It was not easy to
make arrangements to
continue my journey.

1327
00:51:58,317 --> 00:51:59,550
- [Tom] It's a mobile home.

1328
00:51:59,550 --> 00:52:00,918
- [Greta] A great
deal of confusion.

1329
00:52:00,918 --> 00:52:02,287
- [Tom] Filled with Lazy Boys.

1330
00:52:02,287 --> 00:52:03,655
- [Greta] Plane
reservations were scarce.

1331
00:52:03,655 --> 00:52:06,257
However, I was finally
successful and was able to board

1332
00:52:06,257 --> 00:52:08,193
another plane for Johannesburg.

1333
00:52:08,193 --> 00:52:10,828
At last I was on my
way to join my father.

1334
00:52:10,828 --> 00:52:12,697
- [Tom] We're on our way.

1335
00:52:12,697 --> 00:52:14,432
- [Greta] It's
necessary to fly over

1336
00:52:14,432 --> 00:52:16,300
the dense African jungle.

1337
00:52:16,300 --> 00:52:17,535
- [Tom] And do a lot
of voiceover work.

1338
00:52:17,535 --> 00:52:18,737
- [Greta] I engaged
in a conversation

1339
00:52:18,737 --> 00:52:20,072
with a very lovely woman.

1340
00:52:20,072 --> 00:52:21,507
- [Tom] That I didn't like.

1341
00:52:21,507 --> 00:52:24,108
- Of course they will be calling
up John and Herbert both.

1342
00:52:25,543 --> 00:52:28,880
Seems so strange, their father
was killed in the last war.

1343
00:52:28,880 --> 00:52:30,048
- [Joel] That's great.

1344
00:52:30,048 --> 00:52:30,982
- [Tom] Yeah that's
great, now put

1345
00:52:30,982 --> 00:52:33,318
a sock in it will ya granny?

1346
00:52:33,318 --> 00:52:35,753
- When you've lived as
long as I have child

1347
00:52:35,753 --> 00:52:38,657
you'll find it
never pays to worry.

1348
00:52:38,657 --> 00:52:42,793
I used to worry terribly
about everything.

1349
00:52:42,793 --> 00:52:45,097
Little things and big things.

1350
00:52:45,097 --> 00:52:48,400
- [Joel] Orange things
and paisley things.

1351
00:52:48,400 --> 00:52:50,535
- What on earth's
the matter with you?

1352
00:52:50,535 --> 00:52:52,103
We all be dead soon enough.

1353
00:52:52,103 --> 00:52:53,070
- [Tom] Yeah sure, hey my
skull's starting to hurt,

1354
00:52:53,070 --> 00:52:54,572
could you clam up?

1355
00:52:54,572 --> 00:52:57,442
- Hey what is this the
airplane of Dr. Calligeri?

1356
00:52:57,442 --> 00:52:59,677
- [Joel] Bizarre.

1357
00:52:59,677 --> 00:53:01,178
Captain and I are out of drinks.

1358
00:53:01,178 --> 00:53:02,747
- Ladies and gentlemen we
have just received word

1359
00:53:02,747 --> 00:53:04,615
over the wireless that
His Majesty's government

1360
00:53:04,615 --> 00:53:06,718
has declared war on Germany.

1361
00:53:06,718 --> 00:53:09,120
- So it's happy
hour until we land.

1362
00:53:09,120 --> 00:53:10,555
(cheers)

1363
00:53:10,555 --> 00:53:12,890
- Every attempt to reach
Johannesburg as per schedule.

1364
00:53:15,027 --> 00:53:16,427
- [Tom] That oughta hold 'em.

1365
00:53:16,427 --> 00:53:17,828
- Well it's come.

1366
00:53:18,963 --> 00:53:20,832
- May the Lord have
mercy on us all.

1367
00:53:20,832 --> 00:53:23,868
- [Tom] Well I think
he does accept for you.

1368
00:53:23,868 --> 00:53:24,802
- [Joel] Stop her
she's got a gun!

1369
00:53:24,802 --> 00:53:26,470
She's got a gun!
- Look out!

1370
00:53:26,470 --> 00:53:29,573
- I think you'll
all want to join me.

1371
00:53:30,508 --> 00:53:34,412
♪ It's a dance of death, death ♪

1372
00:53:34,412 --> 00:53:37,248
♪ It's a dance of death ♪

1373
00:53:37,248 --> 00:53:39,150
(soft music)

1374
00:53:39,150 --> 00:53:41,452
- [Tom] God save the Queen.

1375
00:53:41,452 --> 00:53:44,388
- I figured I was seeing Betty
and the kids for Christmas.

1376
00:53:44,388 --> 00:53:45,757
- What about your wife?

1377
00:53:45,757 --> 00:53:48,192
- Wonder how long
it will be now?

1378
00:53:48,192 --> 00:53:49,460
At least I can send him

1379
00:53:49,460 --> 00:53:51,195
a picture of his dad
in a RAF uniform.

1380
00:53:51,195 --> 00:53:53,332
- [Tom] Instead of
that darn dress.

1381
00:53:56,100 --> 00:53:58,135
Meanwhile on yet another plane.

1382
00:54:00,305 --> 00:54:03,040
Uh oh, when you stopped
for fuel did you?

1383
00:54:03,040 --> 00:54:03,875
Huh?

1384
00:54:07,478 --> 00:54:09,913
- [Joel] We're in trouble,
how's the model doing?

1385
00:54:09,913 --> 00:54:12,217
- [Tom] Not too good.

1386
00:54:12,217 --> 00:54:13,585
- When you were in flight school

1387
00:54:13,585 --> 00:54:15,887
did they teach
you how to scream?

1388
00:54:15,887 --> 00:54:18,623
(dramatic music)

1389
00:54:22,127 --> 00:54:24,295
- [Tom] So you wanna
tell 'em or should I?

1390
00:54:24,295 --> 00:54:27,798
(dramatic music)

1391
00:54:27,798 --> 00:54:28,967
Uh oh.

1392
00:54:28,967 --> 00:54:30,535
- She's dropping
fast, I better go warn

1393
00:54:30,535 --> 00:54:31,937
the passengers to fasten
their safety belts.

1394
00:54:31,937 --> 00:54:34,505
- [Joel] Yeah like
that's gonna help.

1395
00:54:34,505 --> 00:54:35,840
- [Tom] Airport 42.

1396
00:54:37,508 --> 00:54:40,978
- Steve, nevermind, I got
it, kinda my fault, sorry.

1397
00:54:42,247 --> 00:54:43,682
Sorry.

1398
00:54:43,682 --> 00:54:45,150
- [Tom] Big drag.

1399
00:54:45,150 --> 00:54:47,652
- [Greta] By some miracle
I was the only survivor.

1400
00:54:47,652 --> 00:54:48,853
- [Tom] By some
plot contrivance.

1401
00:54:48,853 --> 00:54:51,488
- [Greta] When I came
to it was morning.

1402
00:54:51,488 --> 00:54:54,658
I didn't know where I was, or
how I was going to get help.

1403
00:54:54,658 --> 00:54:57,762
- Thanks to my Halston
I still looked fabulous.

1404
00:54:57,762 --> 00:54:59,563
- [Greta] Started wandering
through the jungle

1405
00:54:59,563 --> 00:55:01,098
to try and get back
to civilization.

1406
00:55:01,098 --> 00:55:03,000
- [Joel] I find that
travel really broadens you.

1407
00:55:03,000 --> 00:55:05,570
(dramatic music)

1408
00:55:05,570 --> 00:55:08,005
- I met neat people like
Roddy McDowell, and you know,

1409
00:55:08,005 --> 00:55:09,573
it's really true what they say.

1410
00:55:10,742 --> 00:55:13,277
- [Tom] Ooh, that monkey
gave me such a chill.

1411
00:55:13,277 --> 00:55:16,047
(dramatic music)

1412
00:55:21,585 --> 00:55:24,155
- [Joel] Well you know what
I think this forest needs

1413
00:55:24,155 --> 00:55:25,790
is a woman's touch.

1414
00:55:27,158 --> 00:55:29,560
(soft music)

1415
00:55:31,228 --> 00:55:34,332
- There I was surrounded
by salad fixings for miles,

1416
00:55:34,332 --> 00:55:36,802
and no orange
vinaigrette in sight.

1417
00:55:36,802 --> 00:55:39,570
(dramatic music)

1418
00:55:42,207 --> 00:55:45,477
- [Joel] Hey toots, it's me
Satan, catch ya later, ya know?

1419
00:55:45,477 --> 00:55:48,245
(dramatic music)

1420
00:55:49,647 --> 00:55:51,750
- [Tom] Suddenly there
I was, in front of

1421
00:55:51,750 --> 00:55:54,285
a rear projection screen,
you know how I hate those.

1422
00:55:54,285 --> 00:55:56,220
(growling)

1423
00:55:56,220 --> 00:55:57,688
- Kitty.

1424
00:55:57,688 --> 00:55:59,757
- [Tom] I screamed and that
seemed to help our relationship.

1425
00:56:01,458 --> 00:56:06,330
- [Joel] Oh darn, oh what
a bad time to break a heel.

1426
00:56:09,033 --> 00:56:10,935
Oh, oh, daddy.

1427
00:56:10,935 --> 00:56:13,705
(dramatic music)

1428
00:56:16,673 --> 00:56:19,210
- Then I came upon a
sanitation landfill,

1429
00:56:19,210 --> 00:56:21,747
I knew civilization
must be near.

1430
00:56:21,747 --> 00:56:24,482
(dramatic music)

1431
00:56:26,417 --> 00:56:28,720
- [Greta] It wasn't long that
I started into the jungle

1432
00:56:28,720 --> 00:56:31,422
that I was confronted
by a group of natives.

1433
00:56:31,422 --> 00:56:33,725
I was really frightened then.

1434
00:56:33,725 --> 00:56:36,460
- [Joel] You can't tell
from this shot, but I was.

1435
00:56:36,460 --> 00:56:37,495
- [Greta] When suddenly
they started to kneel

1436
00:56:37,495 --> 00:56:39,430
in an attitude of worship.

1437
00:56:39,430 --> 00:56:44,435
I didn't know why but I felt
safer, so mustering my courage.

1438
00:56:45,503 --> 00:56:46,737
- [Tom] I began kicking
them repeatedly.

1439
00:56:47,972 --> 00:56:50,073
- Take me to your village.

1440
00:56:50,073 --> 00:56:50,908
Huh?
- Huh?

1441
00:56:52,810 --> 00:56:55,380
- [Tom] What the? You get that?

1442
00:56:58,315 --> 00:56:59,617
- Take me to your village.

1443
00:57:01,920 --> 00:57:04,288
- She thinks we speak english.

1444
00:57:04,288 --> 00:57:07,092
- [Tom] Yeah sister,
don't give me any crap.

1445
00:57:07,092 --> 00:57:08,527
- You

1446
00:57:08,527 --> 00:57:09,360
- [Tom] Me.

1447
00:57:09,360 --> 00:57:10,195
- Take me.

1448
00:57:10,195 --> 00:57:11,028
- [Tom] Take you.

1449
00:57:11,028 --> 00:57:12,530
- To your village.

1450
00:57:12,530 --> 00:57:13,297
- [Tom] Oh you want us to
take you to our village.

1451
00:57:13,297 --> 00:57:14,532
- House, house.

1452
00:57:16,767 --> 00:57:18,168
(speaking foreign language)

1453
00:57:18,168 --> 00:57:21,605
- [Tom] I'm perplexed by
charmed by this plucky stranger.

1454
00:57:21,605 --> 00:57:22,773
- We eat tonight.

1455
00:57:25,943 --> 00:57:26,945
- [Tom] Oopsie daisy.

1456
00:57:29,280 --> 00:57:32,350
(speaking gibberish)

1457
00:57:33,417 --> 00:57:36,187
What's going on,
somebody drop a contact?

1458
00:57:36,187 --> 00:57:37,355
Here let me help you.

1459
00:57:41,425 --> 00:57:45,095
(speaking foreign language)

1460
00:57:47,298 --> 00:57:49,600
You caught us at a bad
time, all of our suits

1461
00:57:49,600 --> 00:57:52,170
are out at the cleaners and it
gets kinda randy around here

1462
00:57:52,170 --> 00:57:54,372
when all of the women
are away, you understand.

1463
00:57:54,372 --> 00:57:58,042
(speaking foreign language)

1464
00:58:01,778 --> 00:58:04,648
- Well here's the first
problem, she's covered with fur,

1465
00:58:05,717 --> 00:58:06,517
give me a razor.

1466
00:58:07,852 --> 00:58:10,622
- [Greta] She was a very
sick girl, and only then

1467
00:58:10,622 --> 00:58:13,223
did I realize that they
wanted me to help her.

1468
00:58:13,223 --> 00:58:15,560
- [Tom] I'm stared of
her, that seemed to help.

1469
00:58:17,562 --> 00:58:18,797
Does this story have a point?

1470
00:58:18,797 --> 00:58:20,965
- When Wanama recovered
the natives were sure

1471
00:58:20,965 --> 00:58:24,435
that I was a goddess,
when Chief Umbanga died

1472
00:58:24,435 --> 00:58:26,303
Ulanga the witch
doctor tried to poison

1473
00:58:26,303 --> 00:58:29,140
the natives against me,
but he wasn't successful.

1474
00:58:29,140 --> 00:58:31,042
- Well do they still believe
that you're a goddess?

1475
00:58:31,042 --> 00:58:32,277
- That's another flashback.

1476
00:58:32,277 --> 00:58:33,812
- I was deceiving them
Ulanga the witch doctor

1477
00:58:33,812 --> 00:58:35,647
would make short work of me.

1478
00:58:35,647 --> 00:58:37,315
- Aha, I'm beginning
to get all this now.

1479
00:58:37,315 --> 00:58:39,350
But why did you have
Bob sentenced to death?

1480
00:58:39,350 --> 00:58:40,918
- You don't think I
intended to carry that

1481
00:58:40,918 --> 00:58:41,887
sentence out do you?

1482
00:58:41,887 --> 00:58:42,853
- [Joel] We did.

1483
00:58:42,853 --> 00:58:43,788
- [Tom] I was counting on it.

1484
00:58:43,788 --> 00:58:44,955
- I was stalling for time.

1485
00:58:44,955 --> 00:58:45,890
- Smart girl.

1486
00:58:45,890 --> 00:58:47,158
- [Tom] You little minx.

1487
00:58:48,593 --> 00:58:51,128
- [Greta] I had to do it, if
the natives thought otherwise

1488
00:58:51,128 --> 00:58:52,663
we'd all be dead.

1489
00:58:52,663 --> 00:58:56,033
- Well that gives us just
seven days to get out of here.

1490
00:58:56,033 --> 00:58:57,868
- Your plane is it alright?

1491
00:58:57,868 --> 00:58:59,103
- [Tom] Oh it's terrific.

1492
00:58:59,103 --> 00:59:00,305
- [Mike] Now it's
in a little clearing

1493
00:59:00,305 --> 00:59:01,238
about a mile from where
your plane crashed.

1494
00:59:01,238 --> 00:59:02,440
- Must be the accident zone.

1495
00:59:02,440 --> 00:59:04,508
- Trust me, obey my
every command, no matter

